---@meta
-- Generated by rs3-api-types from https://developer.runescape.com/rs/ui/interactive_components/button.html;
-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---Buttons are the most basic interactive component available to users, triggering an action when clicked on. They can
---also be flagged as toggles, which changes the visual representation to reflect both on and off statuses.
---
---Additionally, buttons can also be configured to react to user inputs in different ways, for example, deferring the
---button press action until the button has been released as opposed to immediately triggering it on a click-down event.
---
---See ui.TriggerMode for more information on the available input handling modes.
---
---Custom Visuals: Using custom or plugin-provided sprites is supported, however the provided sprite must represent a
---spritesheet containing all of the potential states in a vertical layout using the following order - `default`,
---`mouseover`, `pressed`, `disabled`, `toggled`, `toggled + mouseover`, `toggled + pressed`, `toggled + disabled`.
---
---Warning: Toggle states can be left blank on the sprite in the event that sprite will never be used for toggle
---buttons, however it's recommended to author those regardless to allow reusing that sprite with other button types.
---@class ui.Button : ui.Component
---@field label string Text to display as this button's label, aliases `text.content`.
---@field isToggled boolean Whether or not the button is toggled currently. Always false for non-toggle buttons.
---@field canToggle boolean Controls whether this button can be toggled or not.
---@field mode ui.TriggerMode Describes how user interactions are handled by this button.
---@field associatedObjectID integer Numeric ID for the object associated with this component, or -1 if no associated object exists.
---@field associatedObjectQuantity integer The quantity for the object associated with this component.
---@field showAssociatedObjectText boolean Controls whether the button's label should be replaced with the associated object's text. Defaults to the actual label text if there's no associated object, or if it's invalid.
---@field showAssociatedObjectSprite boolean Controls whether the sprite for the associated object will be displayed on top of the button's sprite. Does nothing if there's no associated object, or if it's invalid.
---@field contentMargin ui.Margin Margin used to determine the label region for the button.
---@field text ui.TextData Button label parameters.
---@field sprite ui.SpriteData Button sprite parameters.
ui.Button = {}

---Creates a new button on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this button in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Button # The newly created button. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Button.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Associates an object with this component, making it use the object's name and optionally it's quantity as the
---displayed contents for this component.
---@param objectID integer Numeric ID for the object to associate with this component.
---@param quantity? Long The quantity for the object to associate with this component.
function ui.Button:SetAssociatedObject(objectID, quantity) end

---Contains the various options for how a button could be triggered by a user or the application.
---@class ui.TriggerMode
---@field ONPRESS_FINISH ui.TriggerMode The button's action will be triggered once the button press animation finishes.
---@field ONPRESS ui.TriggerMode The button's action will be triggered immediately after the user clicks/taps on the button.
---@field ONRELEASE ui.TriggerMode The button's action will only be triggered once the user releases the click/tap on the button.
---@field REPEAT ui.TriggerMode The button's action will trigger similarly to ONPRESS and will repeat every so often while held down.
ui.TriggerMode = {}
